1
00:00:14,541 --> 00:00:16,541
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:43,708 --> 00:00:47,375
MIRACLES OF THE ER

3
00:00:49,458 --> 00:00:51,207
LILLIAN
CUTE DATE LOOKS

4
00:00:51,208 --> 00:00:53,290
[playful music playing]

5
00:00:53,291 --> 00:00:54,374
Look at this.

6
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:57,207
This says there's a rule of three
with dating.

7
00:00:57,208 --> 00:01:01,665
The rules of dating state, "Three dates
for three hours for three months."

8
00:01:01,666 --> 00:01:05,499
If there's no spark after three days,
that means it's never gonna happen.

9
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,624
- Do you need three dates?
- [Hsiang-chun] Mmm-hmm.

10
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:11,790
- I'm pretty certain after one, you'd know.
- [Chih-cheng] Yeah, why wait for three?

11
00:01:11,791 --> 00:01:14,957
It's not hard to find someone
who's gonna kiss you on the first date.

12
00:01:14,958 --> 00:01:17,124
Well, someone else
was bringing me breakfast everyday

13
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:18,999
- and desperate to win me over.
- [snickers]

14
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,165
Well, someone else was crying to me
about their work stress

15
00:01:21,166 --> 00:01:22,500
and asking me for drinks.

16
00:01:24,458 --> 00:01:25,999
- You got down and begged.
- I slipped.

17
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,374
Yeah, and I tripped and fell on you.

18
00:01:27,375 --> 00:01:28,832
[in unison] It was pathetic!

19
00:01:28,833 --> 00:01:31,207
Wow, so in sync.

20
00:01:31,208 --> 00:01:32,541
[both] I'm not in sync...

21
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:35,707
- [Su-ching] Look this way. Say, "cheese."
- [camera shutter clicks]

22
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:37,166
[Chih-cheng] I'm sick of this.

23
00:01:37,791 --> 00:01:39,082
No, I'm sick of this.

24
00:01:39,083 --> 00:01:40,707
- Hsiang-chun, listen up.
- [Hsiang-chun] Mmm?

25
00:01:40,708 --> 00:01:42,957
If someone asks you out
while you're working the night shift,

26
00:01:42,958 --> 00:01:44,916
don't say yes straight away.
Think about it.

27
00:01:45,916 --> 00:01:47,582
Actually, don't think too much.

28
00:01:47,583 --> 00:01:49,790
Or you'll end up like Dr. Chou and Yu-hua.

29
00:01:49,791 --> 00:01:50,875
[Yu-hua] What about me?

30
00:01:53,166 --> 00:01:55,249
- I need the bathroom.
- Yeah, I do, too.

31
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:57,041
[Hsiu-ju] Better get back to work.

32
00:01:58,083 --> 00:02:00,083
[playful music continues playing]

33
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:06,250
[gasps]

34
00:02:07,458 --> 00:02:08,458
"Rules of three."

35
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:10,832
[indistinct chatter]

36
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:12,624
[Hsiang-chun]
Doctor, there's a patient for you.

37
00:02:12,625 --> 00:02:14,540
[Hsiu-ju] They're coming through.
Make way, please!

38
00:02:14,541 --> 00:02:17,540
- [Tung-yen] What have we got?
- [EMT] 16-year-old female, she's fainted.

39
00:02:17,541 --> 00:02:20,707
BP, 109 over 69.
Heart rate's 70. Sat's 90.

40
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:23,541
- Yep. One, two, three.
- [Hsiang-chun grunts]

41
00:02:25,583 --> 00:02:27,500
Hi, miss. What's your name?

42
00:02:28,166 --> 00:02:30,458
- Her name's Tu I-hui.
- Tung-yen.

43
00:02:43,208 --> 00:02:44,665
Get her to a ward.

44
00:02:44,666 --> 00:02:45,916
Right.

45
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:48,165
Are you family? You know what happened?

46
00:02:48,166 --> 00:02:49,832
No, I'm her boss.

47
00:02:49,833 --> 00:02:52,290
She's been saying she's unwell,
going to the bathroom a lot.

48
00:02:52,291 --> 00:02:55,582
And today she fainted,
so I called an ambulance right away.

49
00:02:55,583 --> 00:02:57,457
Did you guys see the bruises here?

50
00:02:57,458 --> 00:02:59,833
I asked her where they're from,
and she wouldn't say.

51
00:03:00,541 --> 00:03:02,541
Her dad just got out of prison recently.

52
00:03:03,208 --> 00:03:04,875
I wonder if it's him that did it.

53
00:03:06,625 --> 00:03:07,875
You haven't seen him yet?

54
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Ah, here he comes.

55
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:13,500
[knocks]

56
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,416
- You needed me?
- [Cheng-chun] Mmm.

57
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,875
Ms. Chang's from PR, she wants to chat.

58
00:03:18,458 --> 00:03:19,457
Hello.

59
00:03:19,458 --> 00:03:21,207
Geng-ming, on your first day,

60
00:03:21,208 --> 00:03:24,833
Dr. He asked you to do an intubation,
which you got wrong, right?

61
00:03:26,166 --> 00:03:27,582
- Yeah.
- [Chia-hsin sighs]

62
00:03:27,583 --> 00:03:30,790
The patient's family
have now made a negligence complaint.

63
00:03:30,791 --> 00:03:33,374
So we'll need to hold
a mediation meeting for the case.

64
00:03:33,375 --> 00:03:37,000
Now, before that takes place,
please don't contact anyone involved.

65
00:03:37,875 --> 00:03:40,458
PR and Legal will act
as the points of contact.

66
00:03:41,666 --> 00:03:43,415
Do they wanna sue me?

67
00:03:43,416 --> 00:03:46,082
[Chia-hsin] We're going to do our best
to prevent that from happening.

68
00:03:46,083 --> 00:03:49,166
But the patient, Wei Sung,
was preparing to do his final concert.

69
00:03:49,750 --> 00:03:52,166
So they might use this
to request compensation.

70
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:56,333
Ms. Chang is just saying
to go about your day as normal, okay?

71
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,166
[sighs] Okay.

72
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:00,583
Thank you.

73
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,500
[Cheng-chun sighs]

74
00:04:05,375 --> 00:04:07,165
Thanks for telling me
about this, Chia-hsin.

75
00:04:07,166 --> 00:04:09,750
And, um, thanks for the coffee.
[chuckles softly]

76
00:04:10,416 --> 00:04:11,416
Sure thing.

77
00:04:12,458 --> 00:04:14,999
And I'll see you
at the musical tomorrow night.

78
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,583
Right. I'll be on time.

79
00:04:20,666 --> 00:04:22,290
[Tung-yen] I think she might have ITP,

80
00:04:22,291 --> 00:04:24,082
- so do a blood smear first.
- Right.

81
00:04:24,083 --> 00:04:25,875
[Tung-yen]
Let me know when you got the results.

82
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:29,541
[telephone ringing]

83
00:04:30,125 --> 00:04:31,208
[Geng-ming] Tung-yen.

84
00:04:31,916 --> 00:04:34,333
What do you think about I-hui's dad?
Should we report it?

85
00:04:35,583 --> 00:04:36,583
[Tung-yen sighs heavily]

86
00:04:38,166 --> 00:04:40,958
- Hey.
- [Tung-yen] Not bruises, it's ITP.

87
00:04:41,958 --> 00:04:44,290
[Geng-ming]
Hsiang-chun, has her family been in yet?

88
00:04:44,291 --> 00:04:46,832
No, not yet. Her boss left.

89
00:04:46,833 --> 00:04:48,666
She doesn't want her dad to come in.

90
00:04:50,125 --> 00:04:51,540
- I'll keep going.
- Mmm. Okay.

91
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:53,957
[machine beeping]

92
00:04:53,958 --> 00:04:55,041
[sighs]

93
00:05:00,875 --> 00:05:02,749
[breathes heavily]

94
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:06,083
[Geng-ming] Hey, don't be scared.
You're in Yang-Da Hospital ER.

95
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:08,208
You fainted at your workplace.

96
00:05:08,916 --> 00:05:10,166
Do you remember that?

97
00:05:11,416 --> 00:05:13,540
[gasps, breathes heavily]

98
00:05:13,541 --> 00:05:15,500
- Hey.
- [I-hui groans]

99
00:05:16,083 --> 00:05:17,583
- [I-hui panicking]
- [Geng-ming] You okay?

100
00:05:19,166 --> 00:05:21,541
Did you contact my father?

101
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:23,125
I-hui.

102
00:05:24,041 --> 00:05:25,665
Do you want me to call a social worker?

103
00:05:25,666 --> 00:05:27,999
[gasps, whimpers] Oh God.

104
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,040
- You guys don't get it. [breathes heavily]
- [cellphone chimes]

105
00:05:31,041 --> 00:05:32,416
[I-hui gasps]

106
00:05:40,375 --> 00:05:42,874
[Chia-hsin] <i>If you see someone
who's not a family member of a patient,</i>

107
00:05:42,875 --> 00:05:47,291
eavesdropping on details of the case
or even recording you, please be careful.

108
00:05:50,958 --> 00:05:52,166
Hey!

109
00:05:53,291 --> 00:05:55,291
[indistinct chatter]

110
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,832
[Geng-ming sighs heavily]

111
00:06:00,833 --> 00:06:03,415
- [Mrs. Tang coughs]
- So you come from Miaoli, is that right?

112
00:06:03,416 --> 00:06:05,790
- [Mrs. Tang] Mmm-hmm.
- I grew up in Miaoli.

113
00:06:05,791 --> 00:06:07,290
- Oh.
- [You-chang] In Tongluo.

114
00:06:07,291 --> 00:06:10,666
[chuckles] We're right nearby. Gongguan.

115
00:06:11,375 --> 00:06:13,790
You're not the Tang family
that makes silk garments?

116
00:06:13,791 --> 00:06:15,207
- A-ha.
- [You-chang chuckles]

117
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:18,415
- We used to buy quilts from you guys.
- [Mrs. Tang] Really? How funny.

118
00:06:18,416 --> 00:06:19,541
- Doctor.
- [Mrs. Tang chuckles]

119
00:06:20,458 --> 00:06:21,708
Oh, Tang Hsi.

120
00:06:22,291 --> 00:06:24,915
Dr. Huang's family used to buy our quilts.

121
00:06:24,916 --> 00:06:26,375
- Amazing.
- [Mrs. Tang] Mmm.

122
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,208
While Dr. Tang is here,
I wanted to tell you both some good news.

123
00:06:30,916 --> 00:06:33,332
I've been able to secure another slot.

124
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:36,874
Mrs. Tang will be able to join
the clinical trial for this new drug

125
00:06:36,875 --> 00:06:38,832
- with fewer side effects.
- [Mrs. Tang gasps]

126
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,040
[hopeful music playing]

127
00:06:40,041 --> 00:06:42,500
That's great. Thank you, doctor.

128
00:06:43,083 --> 00:06:45,665
We're colleagues,
and you're senior doctor's a good friend.

129
00:06:45,666 --> 00:06:48,041
It makes sense to take care of each other.

130
00:06:49,166 --> 00:06:51,749
[nurse] Dr. Huang,
I've got Mr. Shui for you again.

131
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,625
[chuckles] Pardon me.

132
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:57,707
Mr. Shui.

133
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:59,665
[Mr. Shui] Thank you so much
for curing my father.

134
00:06:59,666 --> 00:07:01,749
- [chuckles] Oh no, it's my job.
- This is for you.

135
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,375
You brought me something again?

136
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:06,458
[Mrs. Tang]
Dr. Huang's such a good person.

137
00:07:07,916 --> 00:07:09,666
Learn lots from him.

138
00:07:13,583 --> 00:07:16,415
[Yu-hua on phone] <i>Thanks so much
for letting Tang Hsi's mom join the trial.</i>

139
00:07:16,416 --> 00:07:19,249
[You-chang] No, it's nothing.
I've gotta take care of your junior.

140
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:21,458
[Yu-hua] <i>Are you free tomorrow night?
I'll buy you dinner.</i>

141
00:07:22,625 --> 00:07:23,625
Okay.

142
00:07:24,375 --> 00:07:26,207
[man] Well, we're given
such a short amount of time.

143
00:07:26,208 --> 00:07:28,415
- [woman] Mmm-hmm. Doctor.
- [man] Doctor.

144
00:07:28,416 --> 00:07:30,041
[You-chang] How are things progressing?

145
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
More delays?

146
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:41,291
[man] Dr. Huang, we work overtime
almost every day.

147
00:07:41,916 --> 00:07:44,625
But this is just too much
for us to get through.

148
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,000
I know it's been tough on you.

149
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,500
But this comes from Director Chang.

150
00:07:50,208 --> 00:07:53,875
I can ask him to extend the deadline,
but you'll still need to work hard.

151
00:07:54,375 --> 00:07:55,790
Hmm? All right.

152
00:07:55,791 --> 00:07:57,375
- Thank you, Dr. Huang.
- Thank you, doctor.

153
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:02,541
Doctor, Tu I-hui's pain has gotten worse.

154
00:08:03,125 --> 00:08:04,915
- Her family here?
- [Hsiang-chun] Not yet.

155
00:08:04,916 --> 00:08:07,249
- Give her a shot of ketorolac first.
- Right.

156
00:08:07,250 --> 00:08:09,708
[rapid footsteps receding]

157
00:08:10,708 --> 00:08:13,957
She seems really scared of her dad.
She must be hiding something.

158
00:08:13,958 --> 00:08:15,375
Maybe you should ask her again.

159
00:08:16,041 --> 00:08:17,915
- [light thud]
- [sighs] Geng-ming.

160
00:08:17,916 --> 00:08:20,874
It's my job. She has ITP.

161
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:23,708
[loudly] Could you stop
making up crazy stories about people?

162
00:08:31,250 --> 00:08:33,708
- [groans in pain]
- [machine beeping]

163
00:08:35,666 --> 00:08:38,083
[retches, moans]

164
00:08:40,708 --> 00:08:42,875
[groans]

165
00:08:46,375 --> 00:08:47,458
[Geng-ming] You okay?

166
00:08:48,333 --> 00:08:49,333
[groans]

167
00:08:50,416 --> 00:08:51,416
Fine.

168
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,666
- [Geng-ming sighs]
- [I-hui groans]

169
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
- [I-hui groaning]
- [low tense music playing]

170
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:04,541
[retching]

171
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:25,250
[gel squelching]

172
00:09:26,583 --> 00:09:30,500
[Geng-ming] Tung-yen, pregnant with ITP.
Is there a risk of miscarriage?

173
00:09:33,625 --> 00:09:35,625
[music intensifies]

174
00:09:40,083 --> 00:09:41,416
Do you know that you're pregnant?

175
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:43,250
[breathes heavily]

176
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:46,582
[whimpers]

177
00:09:46,583 --> 00:09:48,249
[I-hui's dad] I'm her dad.
I'm gonna see her.

178
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:50,290
[Hsiu-ju] Mr. Tu, she's being examined.

179
00:09:50,291 --> 00:09:52,832
- I'll tell you when she's done.
- Examine for what?

180
00:09:52,833 --> 00:09:55,332
You need to wait.
Excuse me, this is not on!

181
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:57,540
You're invading patients' privacy.

182
00:09:57,541 --> 00:09:58,665
Mr. Tu!

183
00:09:58,666 --> 00:10:00,665
- I need you to--
- [Geng-ming] Hey!

184
00:10:00,666 --> 00:10:02,374
[I-hui whimpers]

185
00:10:02,375 --> 00:10:04,915
[angrily] So this is where
you've been hiding?

186
00:10:04,916 --> 00:10:06,082
[Tung-yen] Excuse me, sir.

187
00:10:06,083 --> 00:10:08,332
Your daughter's platelet count
is very low.

188
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:09,916
[yells] I don't know what you mean!

189
00:10:10,666 --> 00:10:11,499
- Come on.
- [I-hui yells]

190
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:12,500
Stop, she's pregnant!

191
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:15,333
[I-hui sobbing]

192
00:10:19,333 --> 00:10:20,833
[whimpers]

193
00:10:21,416 --> 00:10:22,790
- You piece of--
- [Tung-yen yells] Hey!

194
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,665
- [I-hui exclaiming]
- [Hsiu-ju] Get away from her!

195
00:10:24,666 --> 00:10:26,707
- You're still a child!
- Sir, calm down!

196
00:10:26,708 --> 00:10:29,540
[Mr. Tu] You can't even take care
of yourself! What do you think'll happen?

197
00:10:29,541 --> 00:10:30,665
[Hsiu-ju] I'll get security.

198
00:10:30,666 --> 00:10:32,832
[Mr. Tu angrily]
You think you can take care of a child?

199
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:34,375
[Tung-yen] Calm, sir!

200
00:10:34,958 --> 00:10:36,207
[Mr. Tu] You fucked up your life!

201
00:10:36,208 --> 00:10:37,790
What do you think you're doing?

202
00:10:37,791 --> 00:10:39,541
[Tung-yen] Please calm down, sir!

203
00:10:42,875 --> 00:10:44,207
[Hsi] Uh, Mr. Jian.

204
00:10:44,208 --> 00:10:48,124
The X-ray shows no sign of fracture,
so I'll just give you some stitches.

205
00:10:48,125 --> 00:10:49,625
Oh, that's great. Thank you.

206
00:10:50,208 --> 00:10:52,124
I'll use saline to clean the area first.

207
00:10:52,125 --> 00:10:54,083
- Uh-huh.
- But it's going to sting a little.

208
00:10:54,708 --> 00:10:57,333
[winces, groans]

209
00:10:57,916 --> 00:11:00,916
- [Hsi] Doing well. Good job. You got it.
- [Mr. Jian wincing]

210
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:04,041
[Hsi] That's it.

211
00:11:06,708 --> 00:11:08,791
Almost done. I'll stitch it up for you.

212
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:10,375
Uh-huh. That's great.

213
00:11:11,625 --> 00:11:12,625
[panting]

214
00:11:15,166 --> 00:11:17,040
[low tense music playing]

215
00:11:17,041 --> 00:11:19,125
[plastic ruffling]

216
00:11:24,833 --> 00:11:26,165
[Hsi] Nurse, we'll be all right here.

217
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:27,250
- Thank you.
- [nurse] Sure.

218
00:11:32,166 --> 00:11:35,124
Dr. Tang, I'm wondering,
why'd you choose the ER?

219
00:11:35,125 --> 00:11:36,208
It's so busy.

220
00:11:36,708 --> 00:11:39,832
If a beautiful girl like you
chose something like dermatology,

221
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,250
you'd get so many clients.

222
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:44,290
You could even be on TV.

223
00:11:44,291 --> 00:11:45,958
Ever thought about that?

224
00:11:47,083 --> 00:11:49,041
[sighs] Not really.

225
00:11:50,041 --> 00:11:53,250
I work in television.
Believe me, the women are beautiful.

226
00:11:53,958 --> 00:11:55,375
But not like this.

227
00:11:55,958 --> 00:11:59,125
I bet you have patients
lining up around the block to see you.

228
00:12:00,166 --> 00:12:01,166
[Mr. Jian chuckles]

229
00:12:05,541 --> 00:12:09,040
Could I ask, did you graduate recently?
How old are you?

230
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:11,125
[music fades]

231
00:12:11,958 --> 00:12:13,207
What do you want?

232
00:12:13,208 --> 00:12:16,708
We got a report of aggressive behavior.
And we'd like to have a talk with you.

233
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,333
- [policeman 1] Hey...
- [Mr. Tu] What's going on?

234
00:12:19,916 --> 00:12:21,791
[angrily] Is it illegal
to talk to my daughter?

235
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:25,166
- [policeman 1] Sir, please calm down.
- [Mr. Tu] Get lost!

236
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:26,999
- I-hui!
- [I-hui gasps]

237
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,999
[Mr. Tu]
Which idiot knocked you up? Tell me!

238
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,958
Excuse me, this is the ER.

239
00:12:33,333 --> 00:12:34,791
Your grades are no good.

240
00:12:35,375 --> 00:12:36,333
You keep running off.

241
00:12:37,416 --> 00:12:39,874
Now you've screwed around
and got yourself knocked up.

242
00:12:39,875 --> 00:12:41,041
Have you no shame?

243
00:12:41,541 --> 00:12:43,625
How'd I get stuck
with a dropkick like you?

244
00:12:45,916 --> 00:12:48,499
Well, I'd rather kill myself
than be your daughter!

245
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,958
- [Yu-hua] Hey!
- Mr. Tu, stay back!

246
00:12:51,666 --> 00:12:52,833
[Mr. Tu grunts angrily]

247
00:12:58,833 --> 00:13:00,000
[Mr. Tu] Come on, out with it!

248
00:13:00,666 --> 00:13:01,666
Who knocked you up?

249
00:13:02,458 --> 00:13:04,749
What are you gonna do?
Walk around high school with a kid?

250
00:13:04,750 --> 00:13:07,125
What would people think?
You're an embarrassment!

251
00:13:07,791 --> 00:13:09,332
What exactly is your plan?

252
00:13:09,333 --> 00:13:12,540
Doctor, you must carry
so much stress with you.

253
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:14,665
[indistinct chatter]

254
00:13:14,666 --> 00:13:17,416
- [Mr. Jian] You work so hard.
- [Mr. Tu] What the hell were you thinking?

255
00:13:18,416 --> 00:13:20,833
[Hsi breathing heavily]

256
00:13:21,625 --> 00:13:26,208
Maybe you would like a massage.

257
00:13:29,875 --> 00:13:32,625
[Hsi trembles]

258
00:13:34,666 --> 00:13:36,666
Of course, I'd cut class.

259
00:13:37,375 --> 00:13:39,582
Everyone knows my dad's been in jail.

260
00:13:39,583 --> 00:13:42,540
[sobs] Why would anyone at school
be friends with me?

261
00:13:42,541 --> 00:13:44,999
And then you're released,
and you're drunk every day.

262
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:49,000
If I feel sick or just upset,
no one's there to look after me.

263
00:13:49,583 --> 00:13:51,541
[sobs, voice breaking] I feel so alone!

264
00:13:52,250 --> 00:13:54,416
I know that I'm a failure.

265
00:13:55,916 --> 00:13:57,916
I know this is my fault.

266
00:13:58,708 --> 00:14:01,416
When you're well enough,
you're getting an abortion.

267
00:14:02,166 --> 00:14:03,916
I can't take care of both of you.

268
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:11,750
[sighs]

269
00:14:12,875 --> 00:14:14,708
Mr. Tu, hold on.

270
00:14:18,708 --> 00:14:20,708
[ominous music builds]

271
00:14:25,083 --> 00:14:27,499
- What are you doing?
- [Mr. Jian exclaims] No! Stop, stop, stop!

272
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:30,249
- It hurts! Please! Stop grabbing my arm!
- [metal clangs]

273
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:33,750
- [yells] Tell me, what were you doing?
- Stop, you're hurting me! [screams]

274
00:14:34,250 --> 00:14:36,000
- [groans in pain]
- [ominous music turns tense]

275
00:14:36,666 --> 00:14:37,832
[exclaims] My head.

276
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:40,416
- [breath trembling]
- [Mr. Jian groaning]

277
00:14:42,208 --> 00:14:43,208
Are you okay?

278
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,500
[music fades]

279
00:15:06,125 --> 00:15:08,457
The curtain blocked what we could see.

280
00:15:08,458 --> 00:15:09,875
Nothing was captured.

281
00:15:10,958 --> 00:15:13,832
We don't need footage.
I was a witness to it.

282
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:15,375
Just a witness?

283
00:15:15,958 --> 00:15:17,332
He says he has concussion,

284
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:19,583
and he's threatening
to sue you for assault.

285
00:15:20,166 --> 00:15:22,166
He was sexually harassing someone.

286
00:15:24,375 --> 00:15:28,708
Could I ask, why did this patient
suddenly think he could touch you?

287
00:15:29,291 --> 00:15:31,583
Did you say something
during the treatment?

288
00:15:32,166 --> 00:15:33,833
[Yu-hua scoffs] Dr. Cheng.

289
00:15:34,416 --> 00:15:36,374
Are you blaming Dr. Tang for this?

290
00:15:36,375 --> 00:15:37,750
Of course not!

291
00:15:38,416 --> 00:15:40,125
I'm just trying to understand.

292
00:15:40,916 --> 00:15:43,041
Could you sit down, please?

293
00:15:43,666 --> 00:15:46,624
I'm just saying,
these perverts are usually all talk.

294
00:15:46,625 --> 00:15:50,165
If Dr. Tang had noticed something
was feeling a little off at the start,

295
00:15:50,166 --> 00:15:53,291
and said something,
she might've avoided this.

296
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,165
We get all kinds of people
every day in the ER.

297
00:15:57,166 --> 00:15:59,749
And Dr. Tang
could take this opportunity to learn--

298
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,749
[sternly] This is not Dr. Tang's fault.

299
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:04,833
No matter what she did
or might not have done.

300
00:16:05,583 --> 00:16:09,124
The situation was caused by the man
who assaulted her.

301
00:16:09,125 --> 00:16:12,624
Research papers indicate
this kind of sudden harassment

302
00:16:12,625 --> 00:16:16,665
can cause a person to completely seize up
and be unable to react.

303
00:16:16,666 --> 00:16:19,540
Dr. Cheng, I thought
you loved research papers.

304
00:16:19,541 --> 00:16:21,915
You're telling me
you really have no idea about this?

305
00:16:21,916 --> 00:16:23,000
All right.

306
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:24,583
We're done.

307
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:29,250
Dr. Tang.

308
00:16:30,166 --> 00:16:33,958
I can assure you,
the hospital is on your side here.

309
00:16:34,458 --> 00:16:37,374
But the situation is,
we have no clear proof.

310
00:16:37,375 --> 00:16:41,000
And he's a TV executive
with the power to influence.

311
00:16:42,125 --> 00:16:43,499
You're a young doctor.

312
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:46,957
If this lawsuit drags on
and it escalates in the future,

313
00:16:46,958 --> 00:16:48,750
it could affect your career.

314
00:16:49,416 --> 00:16:52,291
So I'm advising you
to think very carefully.

315
00:16:52,875 --> 00:16:54,291
Consider the big picture.

316
00:16:54,875 --> 00:16:56,166
- Let's leave it there.
- Dr. Chung.

317
00:16:58,083 --> 00:16:59,916
I'm not sure what "big picture" you mean.

318
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:05,749
But isn't protecting junior doctors
the job of those more senior?

319
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:06,833
I think it is.

320
00:17:07,625 --> 00:17:08,625
Dr. Chou, please.

321
00:17:09,458 --> 00:17:10,791
Mind your attitude.

322
00:17:19,208 --> 00:17:20,208
[sighs]

323
00:17:21,666 --> 00:17:24,375
[gentle music playing]

324
00:17:38,125 --> 00:17:40,125
[gentle music continues playing]

325
00:17:41,791 --> 00:17:43,333
[Hsi hesitates] Doctor, uh, I...

326
00:17:43,958 --> 00:17:45,833
It's fine, it's fine. We've...

327
00:17:46,333 --> 00:17:48,208
- got it all covered here.
- [Chao-i] Mmm-hmm.

328
00:17:48,833 --> 00:17:50,541
So go home and rest up.

329
00:17:51,250 --> 00:17:55,165
- Sorry, I... I increased your workload.
- It's fine.

330
00:17:55,166 --> 00:17:56,250
[Chao-i] You did nothing.

331
00:17:56,833 --> 00:17:58,666
That asshole is the only one to blame.

332
00:18:00,625 --> 00:18:01,708
She's right.

333
00:18:02,708 --> 00:18:03,707
[Yu-hua sighs]

334
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:08,083
Now I want you to remember,
we'll always be on your side.

335
00:18:08,625 --> 00:18:11,541
We're not gonna let them bully you. Okay?

336
00:18:12,083 --> 00:18:13,083
[Hsi] Mmm.

337
00:18:13,875 --> 00:18:16,791
You need to talk to someone,
I'll be there.

338
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:18,833
Okay.

339
00:18:20,125 --> 00:18:21,125
Bye-bye.

340
00:18:23,708 --> 00:18:24,708
[Yu-hua sighs]

341
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:29,500
Is this ever gonna stop happening?

342
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:33,000
[Chao-i] No, I don't think it will.

343
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,708
You remember what you said

344
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:39,082
when I was your R1?

345
00:18:39,083 --> 00:18:40,666
No. What was it?

346
00:18:41,166 --> 00:18:42,125
[Chao-i] You said,

347
00:18:42,958 --> 00:18:43,958
"Being upset

348
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:46,375
is all right."

349
00:18:46,958 --> 00:18:48,583
"But don't let them defeat you."

350
00:18:55,166 --> 00:18:56,166
[chuckles]

351
00:19:00,875 --> 00:19:02,875
- [music fades]
- [Yu-hua chuckles softly]

352
00:19:07,041 --> 00:19:08,041
[footsteps approaching]

353
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:10,165
- What do you want?
- [boy gasps]

354
00:19:10,166 --> 00:19:12,499
Hey! Why are you doing this?

355
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:14,958
Don't play dumb, all right?
Why did you film me?

356
00:19:15,541 --> 00:19:18,082
- It's not about you.
- [Geng-ming] I don't believe you.

357
00:19:18,083 --> 00:19:19,083
[boy groans]

358
00:19:19,875 --> 00:19:21,500
Okay. Watch.

359
00:19:32,666 --> 00:19:33,666
What do you want with her?

360
00:19:44,791 --> 00:19:45,791
[telephone ringing]

361
00:19:46,583 --> 00:19:47,583
[Geng-ming] Mr. Tu.

362
00:19:54,541 --> 00:19:55,541
[boy sighs]

363
00:19:57,583 --> 00:19:58,791
My name's Kai-hsiang.

364
00:19:59,833 --> 00:20:01,125
I'm I-hui's boyfriend.

365
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,750
You're the one who knocked her up.

366
00:20:06,791 --> 00:20:08,749
- [softly] I'm sorry.
- [yells] Don't try it!

367
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:10,166
- You're sorry?
- [loudly] Listen to me!

368
00:20:12,083 --> 00:20:13,375
I'm serious about this.

369
00:20:14,916 --> 00:20:18,124
Whatever she decides to do,
I will support her.

370
00:20:18,125 --> 00:20:20,457
- Oh, bullshit!
- [Geng-ming] Could you stop?

371
00:20:20,458 --> 00:20:23,415
You have no idea
what it takes to raise a child!

372
00:20:23,416 --> 00:20:26,124
When she got sick, if something happened,

373
00:20:26,125 --> 00:20:28,457
I'd get so worried I couldn't sleep.

374
00:20:28,458 --> 00:20:30,374
[soft music playing]

375
00:20:30,375 --> 00:20:32,708
'Cause I knew I couldn't do anything.

376
00:20:33,291 --> 00:20:34,666
I couldn't protect her.

377
00:20:36,125 --> 00:20:37,708
Or be there when she needed me.

378
00:20:39,708 --> 00:20:40,708
[I-hui] Dad?

379
00:20:52,791 --> 00:20:54,916
- [Mr. Tu sniffles]
- [I-hui] I want to keep the baby.

380
00:20:58,375 --> 00:20:59,375
We'd...

381
00:20:59,958 --> 00:21:02,583
We could be like what a normal family is.

382
00:21:03,375 --> 00:21:05,208
[breathes heavily]

383
00:21:10,958 --> 00:21:13,541
[Mr. Tu sniffles, sighs heavily]

384
00:21:19,791 --> 00:21:21,791
[sobs]

385
00:21:25,250 --> 00:21:26,916
[Mr. Tu] Focus on recovering.

386
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:29,833
After that, we can talk about the baby.

387
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:36,541
[I-hui sniffles, chuckles]

388
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:42,958
[Kai-hsiang] Thank you, doctor.

389
00:21:44,833 --> 00:21:46,124
Now, go home and rest.

390
00:21:46,125 --> 00:21:47,208
Right.

391
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:49,625
Come on.

392
00:21:50,625 --> 00:21:52,665
[music fades]

393
00:21:52,666 --> 00:21:54,250
Oh, doctor.

394
00:21:54,833 --> 00:21:56,166
I wanted to tell you something.

395
00:21:57,416 --> 00:22:00,083
[siren wailing in distance]

396
00:22:01,166 --> 00:22:02,166
[whispering] Hey.

397
00:22:02,833 --> 00:22:04,791
- Hey, why don't you just do it?
- [mouse clicks]

398
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,083
- One try won't hurt.
- [telephone ringing]

399
00:22:09,166 --> 00:22:10,291
Dr. Chiang?

400
00:22:11,333 --> 00:22:12,333
Um...

401
00:22:13,208 --> 00:22:15,707
You wanna go
for a late-night snack after work?

402
00:22:15,708 --> 00:22:17,708
[playful music builds]

403
00:22:19,875 --> 00:22:20,875
I'm not hungry.

404
00:22:22,250 --> 00:22:23,250
[thuds]

405
00:22:24,958 --> 00:22:26,166
[Tung-yen sighs]

406
00:22:27,458 --> 00:22:30,166
[Su-ching] Mmm, don't worry.
Two more chances.

407
00:22:32,583 --> 00:22:34,915
Do I really, though? [sighs]

408
00:22:34,916 --> 00:22:36,333
Yeah, I'm sure you will.

409
00:22:37,666 --> 00:22:39,500
- You think?
- For sure.

410
00:22:40,166 --> 00:22:41,249
[both chuckle]

411
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:43,165
I'll take you for a late-night snack.

412
00:22:43,166 --> 00:22:44,874
- You can have whatever you want.
- Ice cream.

413
00:22:44,875 --> 00:22:45,957
[both chuckle]

414
00:22:45,958 --> 00:22:47,165
[Su-ching exclaims softly]

415
00:22:47,166 --> 00:22:49,083
- It's okay.
- [Hsiang-chun sighs]

416
00:23:04,958 --> 00:23:05,958
[box thuds softly]

417
00:23:08,541 --> 00:23:10,874
Oh, I'm Dr. Lin.

418
00:23:10,875 --> 00:23:13,165
I treated you when you were in the ER.

419
00:23:13,166 --> 00:23:15,207
I brought pears.
They're good for your lungs.

420
00:23:15,208 --> 00:23:17,666
[hesitates] I'm so sorry
for the mistake I made,

421
00:23:18,250 --> 00:23:19,250
with the intubation.

422
00:23:22,750 --> 00:23:25,000
[Wei Sung coughing]

423
00:23:40,958 --> 00:23:42,750
[screams]

424
00:23:43,833 --> 00:23:44,833
[exclaims]

425
00:23:45,750 --> 00:23:46,749
[sighs heavily]

426
00:23:46,750 --> 00:23:48,833
[pensive music playing]

427
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:56,457
[Chien-te] Take them away.
We don't want them.

428
00:23:56,458 --> 00:23:58,791
[hesitates] I just wanted to apologize
to Mr. Wei.

429
00:24:00,916 --> 00:24:02,415
[angrily] We don't want them. Take them!

430
00:24:02,416 --> 00:24:04,541
How can he play his farewell concert now?

431
00:24:05,541 --> 00:24:08,125
Because of your failure,
my dad is lying here.

432
00:24:09,541 --> 00:24:13,082
The fans won't see him perform.
The staff's hard work has gone to waste.

433
00:24:13,083 --> 00:24:15,999
A fruit basket and an apology
won't make up for it.

434
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,457
Nice try. See you in court.

435
00:24:18,458 --> 00:24:19,833
Now, get out!

436
00:24:20,958 --> 00:24:22,166
I'm sorry.

437
00:24:27,416 --> 00:24:28,416
[sighs]

438
00:24:34,541 --> 00:24:35,874
MOM: SON, WHAT'S UP?

439
00:24:35,875 --> 00:24:38,540
I COOKED CURRY RICE TODAY
COME HOME EARLIER AND EAT

440
00:24:38,541 --> 00:24:40,082
SON, WHAT'S UP?

441
00:24:40,083 --> 00:24:42,415
[Geng-ming's mom] <i>Hi, Geng-ming.
Sorry I missed your call.</i>

442
00:24:42,416 --> 00:24:45,166
<i>I was collecting the laundry.
You doing okay?</i>

443
00:24:45,666 --> 00:24:46,666
[chuckles]

444
00:24:50,833 --> 00:24:52,166
Mom, I'm all good.

445
00:24:52,750 --> 00:24:55,249
Actually, I did a great job today.

446
00:24:55,250 --> 00:24:58,624
We had a female patient.
Nobody knew what was wrong with her.

447
00:24:58,625 --> 00:25:00,458
But we found out later she was pregnant.

448
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:02,041
And what else?

449
00:25:02,541 --> 00:25:05,249
One of the other doctors,
her name's Tang Hsi,

450
00:25:05,250 --> 00:25:07,915
and she had this horrible patient...

451
00:25:07,916 --> 00:25:09,124
[tapping container]

452
00:25:09,125 --> 00:25:10,207
[loudly] Siaohua!

453
00:25:10,208 --> 00:25:12,124
[soft music playing]

454
00:25:12,125 --> 00:25:13,791
I've got some food.

455
00:25:20,458 --> 00:25:21,625
[softly] Oh, here.

456
00:25:23,208 --> 00:25:24,791
Uh-huh. Here.

457
00:25:25,583 --> 00:25:27,833
There you go. Tastes good, huh?

458
00:25:29,583 --> 00:25:31,624
[Geng-ming]
The patient's boyfriend filmed this.

459
00:25:31,625 --> 00:25:33,583
[I-hui on video] <i>Of course, I cut class.</i>

460
00:25:34,333 --> 00:25:36,333
<i>Everyone knows my dad's been in jail.</i>

461
00:25:36,916 --> 00:25:39,040
- <i>Why would anyone...</i>
- This is enough to take him to court.

462
00:25:39,041 --> 00:25:41,999
- Make him pay.
- [I-hui] <i>...drunk every day.</i>

463
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:45,457
<i>If I feel sick or just upset,
no one's there to look after me.</i>

464
00:25:45,458 --> 00:25:46,541
I'm not sure.

465
00:25:47,416 --> 00:25:49,708
Do I wanna be a second-year resident

466
00:25:50,333 --> 00:25:52,416
who's already facing a lawsuit

467
00:25:53,333 --> 00:25:55,000
that might go on forever?

468
00:25:56,916 --> 00:25:58,416
I need to think about it.

469
00:26:01,333 --> 00:26:03,415
- I've got a question for you.
- [Geng-ming] Mmm.

470
00:26:03,416 --> 00:26:06,999
How come Yang-Da chose a student
that didn't get good grades?

471
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,624
Are your parents rich or something?

472
00:26:08,625 --> 00:26:09,791
[chuckles softly]

473
00:26:10,833 --> 00:26:12,291
My dad does massage.

474
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,290
My sis drives cabs.

475
00:26:14,291 --> 00:26:16,124
You didn't get here
through connections, then.

476
00:26:16,125 --> 00:26:17,583
[chuckling] Absolutely not.

477
00:26:18,291 --> 00:26:22,082
Well, it's always been hard for me
to hide my rich-kid-nepo-baby aura.

478
00:26:22,083 --> 00:26:24,541
Why did Dr. Chou choose you, then?

479
00:26:28,875 --> 00:26:31,708
[young Geng-ming sobbing] Please. Mister!

480
00:26:32,583 --> 00:26:33,999
[panting]

481
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,749
Save my mom.

482
00:26:35,750 --> 00:26:37,540
[soft music continues playing]

483
00:26:37,541 --> 00:26:39,791
[Geng-ming]
<i>I've actually always looked up to him.</i>

484
00:26:40,458 --> 00:26:43,040
Dr. Chou helped me when I was a kid.

485
00:26:43,041 --> 00:26:44,290
Seriously?

486
00:26:44,291 --> 00:26:45,665
[cat meows]

487
00:26:45,666 --> 00:26:47,915
Yeah, Siaohua believes me.

488
00:26:47,916 --> 00:26:49,749
[Hsi] Don't just give him
some random name.

489
00:26:49,750 --> 00:26:52,332
Well, if they don't have a name,
they won't come when they're called.

490
00:26:52,333 --> 00:26:53,790
Siaohua is so boring.

491
00:26:53,791 --> 00:26:56,999
- I like Siaoming more.
- [Geng-ming gasps softly]

492
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,958
No way, my dad calls me that.

493
00:26:59,541 --> 00:27:01,165
- Siaoming.
- [chuckles]

494
00:27:01,166 --> 00:27:03,625
[cat meowing]

495
00:27:04,208 --> 00:27:06,375
You know, I'm really happy
I met you and Tung-yen.

496
00:27:06,958 --> 00:27:10,541
Yang-Da first and second honors.
I'm so happy I have you two as...

497
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,166
fellow residents.

498
00:27:14,916 --> 00:27:17,041
Well, I'll probably leave ER pretty soon.

499
00:27:17,625 --> 00:27:18,458
Huh?

500
00:27:19,958 --> 00:27:22,583
I guess I didn't imagine
it would be like this.

501
00:27:26,208 --> 00:27:28,957
I'll head off.
Thank you so much for today.

502
00:27:28,958 --> 00:27:30,041
Huh?

503
00:27:30,833 --> 00:27:32,041
- See you soon.
- [Hsi] Mmm-hmm.

504
00:27:36,958 --> 00:27:38,457
[Geng-ming] Did I say something wrong?

505
00:27:38,458 --> 00:27:40,457
[music fades]

506
00:27:40,458 --> 00:27:42,040
- [cutlery clanging]
- [Hsi] The nurses said

507
00:27:42,041 --> 00:27:45,791
you haven't been eating much. Make sure
you keep your nutrients up, okay?

508
00:27:46,333 --> 00:27:49,375
<i>Look how much you ordered.
Will you finish it?</i>

509
00:27:49,958 --> 00:27:51,832
Mmm-hmm. I'll tell you about each one.

510
00:27:51,833 --> 00:27:53,000
[Mrs. Tang chuckling] <i>Okay.</i>

511
00:27:53,583 --> 00:27:55,416
<i>Are you looking after yourself?</i>

512
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:58,040
<i>You've been working so hard.</i>

513
00:27:58,041 --> 00:27:59,915
Oh, Mom, this fish soup's good.

514
00:27:59,916 --> 00:28:03,165
When you get better,
we can go here together, okay?

515
00:28:03,166 --> 00:28:04,624
<i>I'm kind of tired.</i>

516
00:28:04,625 --> 00:28:06,290
<i>I might have a rest.</i>

517
00:28:06,291 --> 00:28:08,999
<i>Ah, take your time with your food.</i>

518
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,832
- Yeah. All right, you go to bed.
- [Mrs. Tang] <i>I will.</i>

519
00:28:11,833 --> 00:28:13,499
- <i>Goodnight.</i>
- Goodnight. Bye-bye.

520
00:28:13,500 --> 00:28:15,083
- [Mrs. Tang] <i>Mmm-hmm.</i>
- [line disconnects]

521
00:28:16,208 --> 00:28:17,290
[customer] Thank you.

522
00:28:17,291 --> 00:28:19,375
[indistinct chatter]

523
00:28:26,875 --> 00:28:28,875
[somber music playing]

524
00:28:32,833 --> 00:28:34,833
[water pattering]

525
00:28:48,750 --> 00:28:50,750
[Hsi sobbing]

526
00:28:58,416 --> 00:29:01,916
[echoing] Could I ask,
did you say something during treatment?

527
00:29:02,666 --> 00:29:05,207
<i>Why did this patient
suddenly think he could touch you?</i>

528
00:29:05,208 --> 00:29:07,457
...with the power to influence.

529
00:29:07,458 --> 00:29:09,291
<i>Consider the big picture.</i>

530
00:29:10,791 --> 00:29:12,791
- [sobbing]
- [water pattering]

531
00:29:20,291 --> 00:29:22,291
[crying]

532
00:29:30,375 --> 00:29:32,375
[siren wailing]

533
00:29:34,833 --> 00:29:35,832
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

534
00:29:35,833 --> 00:29:37,665
- [EMT] Out of the way!
- [Hsiu-ju] New patient!

535
00:29:37,666 --> 00:29:41,207
[EMT] He's 12, 40 kilograms,
short of breath and vomiting. Sat's 85.

536
00:29:41,208 --> 00:29:42,541
Can you tell me your name?

537
00:29:43,250 --> 00:29:45,083
[weakly] Sung Hsiang-yu.

538
00:29:46,333 --> 00:29:47,625
[Geng-ming] Dr. Chou, cyanosis.

539
00:29:48,666 --> 00:29:49,874
[Mrs. Sung] Excuse me.

540
00:29:49,875 --> 00:29:52,999
My son got a fever from a cold last week
and hasn't recovered.

541
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:54,832
- He's having trouble breathing.
- Right, okay.

542
00:29:54,833 --> 00:29:56,290
Mrs. Sung, you need to register.

543
00:29:56,291 --> 00:29:58,375
- We've got it from here.
- [Mrs. Sung sobs]

544
00:29:59,083 --> 00:30:00,625
With me. One, two, three.

545
00:30:02,875 --> 00:30:03,708
Here.

546
00:30:05,208 --> 00:30:07,333
[hissing]

547
00:30:09,666 --> 00:30:10,999
[Hsiu-ju] You're Hsiang-yu, right?

548
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,165
We're gonna take a look at some things.
Just try to relax, okay?

549
00:30:14,166 --> 00:30:16,666
- [Hsiang-yu breathing heavily]
- [machine beeping rapidly]

550
00:30:19,166 --> 00:30:21,166
- [machine alarms]
- [Geng-ming] Dr. Chou, VT.

551
00:30:23,125 --> 00:30:25,665
- [Cheng-chun] Blood pressure.
- [Hsiu-ju] 75 over 38.

552
00:30:25,666 --> 00:30:27,499
Jugular venous distension.

553
00:30:27,500 --> 00:30:29,665
Geng-ming, what's the next step here?

554
00:30:29,666 --> 00:30:30,957
[Geng-ming] Uh...

555
00:30:30,958 --> 00:30:33,832
[mumbling] VT with pulse, but shortness
of breath and low blood pressure.

556
00:30:33,833 --> 00:30:35,415
- Cardioversion!
- [Cheng-chun] And how much?

557
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:37,332
- [hesitates] How much does he weigh?
- 40 kilograms.

558
00:30:37,333 --> 00:30:39,374
- 40 joules, then. Uh-huh.
- [Cheng-chun] Defib.

559
00:30:39,375 --> 00:30:41,124
[rapid footsteps receding]

560
00:30:41,125 --> 00:30:42,833
[Hsiang-yu breathing heavily]

561
00:30:43,875 --> 00:30:45,540
[digital beeps]

562
00:30:45,541 --> 00:30:48,249
Geng-ming, get his mother
to sign the consent form.

563
00:30:48,250 --> 00:30:49,582
Okay, where are we at?

564
00:30:49,583 --> 00:30:51,915
Synchornized cardioversion 40. Wen-chih.

565
00:30:51,916 --> 00:30:54,208
- Ketamine, 40 milligrams, IV push.
- [Wen-chih] Yep.

566
00:30:55,458 --> 00:30:57,957
- Ketamine, 40 milligrams, IV push.
- Correct.

567
00:30:57,958 --> 00:31:00,665
- 40 joules ready.
- [defibrillator charging]

568
00:31:00,666 --> 00:31:01,750
[Yu-hua] Clear.

569
00:31:06,791 --> 00:31:08,791
[breathing heavily]

570
00:31:11,375 --> 00:31:13,291
[machine beeping stabilizes]

571
00:31:14,958 --> 00:31:17,458
Heart rate looks stable for now.
Sinus rhythm.

572
00:31:18,041 --> 00:31:21,874
Another EKG, then do CBC, biochem,
troponin, blood gas, and an X-ray.

573
00:31:21,875 --> 00:31:22,958
- Uh-huh.
- [Hsiu-ju] Right.

574
00:31:24,208 --> 00:31:27,041
- Buddy, you hang in there, okay?
- [Hsiang-yu breathing heavily]

575
00:31:28,500 --> 00:31:31,999
Mrs. Sung, we need you to give
your consent here so we can operate.

576
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:35,957
Well, I'm not sure if I should sign it.
Could you just hold on for a bit?

577
00:31:35,958 --> 00:31:37,540
[Su-ching] Mrs. Sung, take a deep breath.

578
00:31:37,541 --> 00:31:40,041
Now, it's very important
that you decide quickly.

579
00:31:43,458 --> 00:31:45,957
Your son needs you.
You should sign the form.

580
00:31:45,958 --> 00:31:49,707
No, I can't make a decision like this.
I'll call my husband. I'll ask him.

581
00:31:49,708 --> 00:31:50,791
Please, ma'am.

582
00:31:51,291 --> 00:31:52,750
[line ringing]

583
00:31:54,500 --> 00:31:55,665
[sighs]

584
00:31:55,666 --> 00:31:56,750
Doctor.

585
00:31:59,291 --> 00:32:03,040
- That the EKG report?
- Low voltage. Electrical alternans.

586
00:32:03,041 --> 00:32:04,665
Chance of cardiac tamponade.

587
00:32:04,666 --> 00:32:05,666
- Echo.
- [Wen-chih] Right.

588
00:32:08,125 --> 00:32:10,207
[tense music playing]

589
00:32:10,208 --> 00:32:12,250
[machine beeping]

590
00:32:19,375 --> 00:32:20,583
Cardiac tamponade confirmed.

591
00:32:21,166 --> 00:32:22,916
We'll need to do a pericardiocentesis.

592
00:32:23,625 --> 00:32:24,624
Where's the consent form?

593
00:32:24,625 --> 00:32:27,541
- [line connects]
- Love? [sobs] We're in the hospital.

594
00:32:28,125 --> 00:32:30,749
Hsiang-yu suddenly fell sick,
so we went to ER.

595
00:32:30,750 --> 00:32:32,249
They want to perform surgery.

596
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:35,207
They're asking me to sign a form,
but I don't know. What should I do?

597
00:32:35,208 --> 00:32:38,499
- [machine beeping rapidly]
- [Hsiang-yu stops breathing]

598
00:32:38,500 --> 00:32:40,541
[machine alarming]

599
00:32:44,541 --> 00:32:46,583
The patient is unconscious.

600
00:32:48,791 --> 00:32:50,207
No pulse. PEA.

601
00:32:50,208 --> 00:32:51,665
- Perform CPR.
- [Yu-hua] Right.

602
00:32:51,666 --> 00:32:54,249
[Mr. Sung on phone]
<i>What exactly is this emergency surgery?</i>

603
00:32:54,250 --> 00:32:58,541
[sobbing] I'm not sure, um, they just
keep saying I need to sign the form.

604
00:32:59,625 --> 00:33:00,624
- [Cheng-chun] Yu-hua.
- Yeah.

605
00:33:00,625 --> 00:33:03,707
Tell cardiosurgery to prepare for ECMO.
Wen-chih, swap in.

606
00:33:03,708 --> 00:33:05,875
[Wen-chih] Three, two, one. Switch.

607
00:33:10,375 --> 00:33:13,290
- Okay?
- My husband will decide when he gets here.

608
00:33:13,291 --> 00:33:15,666
- Just wait a bit longer.
- [sighs]

609
00:33:16,375 --> 00:33:20,499
Cheng-chun, the last ECMO is being used
by another patient in the ICU.

610
00:33:20,500 --> 00:33:22,541
There are no other machines available.

611
00:33:23,458 --> 00:33:26,957
Doctor, she wants to wait for her husband.
She won't sign the form.

612
00:33:26,958 --> 00:33:30,457
Can't wait. Go get the mother in here.
I'll explain to her what's happening.

613
00:33:30,458 --> 00:33:31,624
Right.

614
00:33:31,625 --> 00:33:33,708
[machine continues beeping rapidly]

615
00:33:37,083 --> 00:33:39,250
[Geng-ming] Dr. Chou, she's here.

616
00:33:40,333 --> 00:33:43,540
[Cheng-chun] The situation's this.
Fluid is compressing your son's heart.

617
00:33:43,541 --> 00:33:46,666
We need to perform an operation
to remove this fluid. Do you consent?

618
00:33:47,958 --> 00:33:50,082
But I just-- Can you wait?

619
00:33:50,083 --> 00:33:52,582
- My husband is on the way now.
- [Cheng-chun] Listen to me.

620
00:33:52,583 --> 00:33:55,083
We have no time to wait.
We need to save your son.

621
00:33:55,791 --> 00:33:58,457
What if this goes badly
and you can't save him?

622
00:33:58,458 --> 00:33:59,790
It will be my fault.

623
00:33:59,791 --> 00:34:02,415
- [sobs] How could I live with that?
- [Cheng-chun] Okay, listen.

624
00:34:02,416 --> 00:34:05,124
The more you drag this out,
the less chance he'll survive.

625
00:34:05,125 --> 00:34:07,916
You need to trust us.
We'll do everything we can, okay?

626
00:34:08,708 --> 00:34:09,749
You know what?

627
00:34:09,750 --> 00:34:13,291
The doctors that are operating,
they really are two of the best here.

628
00:34:14,333 --> 00:34:17,583
- No need to worry. Leave it to them.
- [Mrs. Sung whimpering]

629
00:34:18,333 --> 00:34:19,458
You can trust them.

630
00:34:21,416 --> 00:34:23,416
[sobbing]

631
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:27,000
Doctor.

632
00:34:29,291 --> 00:34:30,291
[breath trembling]

633
00:34:31,791 --> 00:34:32,791
[groans]

634
00:34:34,791 --> 00:34:37,790
- [Mrs. Sung gasps, sighs]
- [exclaims]

635
00:34:37,791 --> 00:34:39,665
- [grunts]
- [Yu-hua] Get her out of here.

636
00:34:39,666 --> 00:34:42,457
- Ask an OBGYN to see her.
- [Hsiu-ju] All right.

637
00:34:42,458 --> 00:34:44,040
- Let's go outside.
- Careful.

638
00:34:44,041 --> 00:34:47,583
We'll go and sit down, okay?
Everything's fine. This way.

639
00:34:48,083 --> 00:34:51,416
- [Cheng-chun] Hold compressions.
- [machine emits a long beep]

640
00:34:54,375 --> 00:34:56,291
[heart beating]

641
00:35:03,208 --> 00:35:05,708
[ominous music builds]

642
00:35:11,666 --> 00:35:13,832
[tense music playing]

643
00:35:13,833 --> 00:35:15,458
[machine beeping rapidly]

644
00:35:18,166 --> 00:35:19,499
[Yu-hua, echoing] Dr. Chou.

645
00:35:19,500 --> 00:35:20,915
[clearly] Dr. Chou.

646
00:35:20,916 --> 00:35:23,250
[machine emits a long beep]

647
00:35:35,041 --> 00:35:37,124
[fluid sloshing]

648
00:35:37,125 --> 00:35:39,208
[tense music turns dramatic]

649
00:35:48,791 --> 00:35:50,791
[music fades]

650
00:35:52,125 --> 00:35:53,665
[dramatic music resumes]

651
00:35:53,666 --> 00:35:55,333
[machine beeping stabilizes]

652
00:35:56,500 --> 00:35:57,791
[Wen-chih] We've got a pulse.

653
00:36:00,791 --> 00:36:02,833
[Cheng-chun]
Yu-hua, I'll leave the rest to you.

654
00:36:03,416 --> 00:36:04,500
[Yu-hua] Uh...

655
00:36:16,541 --> 00:36:18,541
[pensive music playing]

656
00:36:47,333 --> 00:36:50,749
- [man] All right, one more time.
- [boy exclaiming playfully]

657
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:52,082
[man] Okay. Let's go one more time.

658
00:36:52,083 --> 00:36:54,832
- [boy] Mom, Dad, look!
- [man] Come on. Give it another go.

659
00:36:54,833 --> 00:36:57,457
Come on. Okay. One, two, three...

660
00:36:57,458 --> 00:36:59,708
- [Cheng-chun grunts]
- [man exclaims] So high!

661
00:37:00,291 --> 00:37:02,082
[boy] Look, it's so high!

662
00:37:02,083 --> 00:37:03,457
[woman] That's okay. Try again.

663
00:37:03,458 --> 00:37:05,583
- [man] Let's try again.
- [boy] Okay.

664
00:37:06,375 --> 00:37:08,915
- Wow!
- Wow, that was good! That was close.

665
00:37:08,916 --> 00:37:11,499
- [man] Okay, one more time.
- [boy] I can do it!

666
00:37:11,500 --> 00:37:12,790
[man] Okay. [laughs]

667
00:37:12,791 --> 00:37:14,290
[boy] One more.

668
00:37:14,291 --> 00:37:15,999
[woman and boy] Wow!

669
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:18,000
- [man] Wow!
- [woman] That's so good.

670
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:22,000
[gentle music playing]

671
00:37:25,791 --> 00:37:27,332
[Jui, echoing] Hey, mister.

672
00:37:27,333 --> 00:37:28,791
I've got a secret.

673
00:37:29,291 --> 00:37:30,415
What's your secret?

674
00:37:30,416 --> 00:37:32,665
One day, I'll be a doctor, too.

675
00:37:32,666 --> 00:37:34,790
- Sure about that?
- [Jui] Uh-huh.

676
00:37:34,791 --> 00:37:37,833
[Cheng-chun] You gotta work hard.
Pinky promise?

677
00:37:38,416 --> 00:37:39,541
That's it!

678
00:37:42,958 --> 00:37:44,624
[gentle music continues playing]

679
00:37:44,625 --> 00:37:46,625
[Chia-hsin] I wondered
why your seat was still empty.

680
00:37:47,458 --> 00:37:48,583
Guess you needed some air.

681
00:37:50,041 --> 00:37:51,916
- Could've just said that.
- [chuckles softly]

682
00:37:52,708 --> 00:37:53,875
You were focused on the show.

683
00:37:55,166 --> 00:37:57,874
Focused? [scoffs] I almost fell asleep.

684
00:37:57,875 --> 00:38:00,915
- [chuckles]
- [Chia-hsin] My dad's life is so strange.

685
00:38:00,916 --> 00:38:03,416
Why would someone
give him tickets to this show?

686
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,333
I brought this with me.

687
00:38:06,833 --> 00:38:07,958
So I could drink it.

688
00:38:09,208 --> 00:38:11,957
If the show turned out to be boring.

689
00:38:11,958 --> 00:38:13,041
Want some?

690
00:38:13,625 --> 00:38:16,083
- [Cheng-chun] Why did you hide it for?
- [Chia-hsin chuckles softly]

691
00:38:17,333 --> 00:38:20,290
- [Chia-hsin] You want wagyu or lobster?
- [Cheng-chun sighs in relief]

692
00:38:20,291 --> 00:38:21,915
[Cheng-chun]
Well, why do we have to choose?

693
00:38:21,916 --> 00:38:24,000
- [Chia-hsin] Then I want both.
- [Cheng-chun] Okay.

694
00:38:24,750 --> 00:38:26,582
- So do you still think...
- [Yu-hua] Is there anything...

695
00:38:26,583 --> 00:38:28,707
[You-chang] I'd like to eat meat. Steak.

696
00:38:28,708 --> 00:38:29,791
[Yu-hua] Mmm.

697
00:38:30,708 --> 00:38:31,790
Noodles?

698
00:38:31,791 --> 00:38:32,875
[Yu-hua] Hmm.

699
00:38:33,375 --> 00:38:34,708
I think I want...

700
00:38:39,541 --> 00:38:41,291
[comical music builds]

701
00:38:43,750 --> 00:38:44,750
[chuckles awkwardly]

702
00:38:50,458 --> 00:38:52,790
[Chia-hsin]
A toast to this lucky coincidence.

703
00:38:52,791 --> 00:38:54,333
[Cheng-chun and You-chang] Cheers.

704
00:38:56,041 --> 00:38:57,041
[Cheng-chun exhales]

705
00:38:57,750 --> 00:39:02,124
I read an article today that said
people only have three chances in love.

706
00:39:02,125 --> 00:39:05,415
If you had a date three times
and you don't feel that spark,

707
00:39:05,416 --> 00:39:07,874
it'll never happen. You agree with that?

708
00:39:07,875 --> 00:39:10,208
I saw that in the lounge on break.

709
00:39:11,041 --> 00:39:14,124
- But it sounds a bit silly.
- [chuckles] I don't know.

710
00:39:14,125 --> 00:39:17,832
You and Cheng-chun
have known each other for so long.

711
00:39:17,833 --> 00:39:20,165
Don't you think if there was a spark,
you'd be together by now?

712
00:39:20,166 --> 00:39:23,083
- I think three times sounds accurate.
- [Yu-hua clears throat]

713
00:39:24,041 --> 00:39:25,041
[chuckles awkwardly]

714
00:39:26,208 --> 00:39:28,957
Luckily, it's the first date
for me and Cheng-chun.

715
00:39:28,958 --> 00:39:31,250
- [quirky music playing]
- [chuckles softly]

716
00:39:31,833 --> 00:39:33,166
I don't need three times.

717
00:39:33,750 --> 00:39:35,708
It's always love at first sight for me.

718
00:39:36,708 --> 00:39:38,708
And once I know I'm in love, that's it.

719
00:39:40,083 --> 00:39:43,291
Didn't take you for the romantic type.
You believe in "the one"?

720
00:39:43,958 --> 00:39:45,832
[scoffs] He's nuts.

721
00:39:45,833 --> 00:39:49,707
I've tried to tell him.
These days, no one believes in "the one".

722
00:39:49,708 --> 00:39:53,333
[chuckles] Yu-hua,
I had no idea we're so similar.

723
00:39:53,916 --> 00:39:54,916
Cheers to that.

724
00:39:56,750 --> 00:39:57,875
[laughs]

725
00:39:59,458 --> 00:40:00,458
[Chia-hsin] Cheers.

726
00:40:04,458 --> 00:40:06,458
[music fades]

727
00:40:07,291 --> 00:40:08,415
- Cheng-chun?
- [Cheng-chun] Hmm?

728
00:40:08,416 --> 00:40:11,124
- There's a...
- Uh, what?

729
00:40:11,125 --> 00:40:12,665
- [Chia-hsin] I'll get it for you.
- Ah...

730
00:40:12,666 --> 00:40:14,457
Oh, I can... Oh, thank you.

731
00:40:14,458 --> 00:40:15,541
Thank you.

732
00:40:16,500 --> 00:40:17,624
[Cheng-chun chuckles softly]

733
00:40:17,625 --> 00:40:18,708
All gone?

734
00:40:20,125 --> 00:40:21,915
[waitress] Okay, here you go.

735
00:40:21,916 --> 00:40:24,500
- Okay. Thanks.
- [waitress] You're welcome.

736
00:40:28,208 --> 00:40:30,916
- [Cheng-chun] Have some... The lobster.
- Oh, thank you.

737
00:40:32,208 --> 00:40:35,082
- Yu-hua, some lobster.
- Um, thanks, Cheng-chun.

738
00:40:35,083 --> 00:40:36,624
- Oh, hold on.
- Huh?

739
00:40:36,625 --> 00:40:38,207
Yu-hua can't eat shellfish.

740
00:40:38,208 --> 00:40:39,625
Didn't you know that?

741
00:40:40,750 --> 00:40:41,957
[Cheng-chun] Oh...

742
00:40:41,958 --> 00:40:43,333
Here, have some steak.

743
00:40:43,958 --> 00:40:46,041
Oh, thank you. [chuckles softly]

744
00:40:50,166 --> 00:40:52,208
[Chia-hsin] Cheng-chun's the only one
who hasn't said yet.

745
00:40:52,791 --> 00:40:54,833
What kind of love are you looking for?

746
00:40:55,416 --> 00:40:57,249
We don't need to go there.

747
00:40:57,250 --> 00:40:59,083
Well, hey, come on.

748
00:41:05,458 --> 00:41:08,541
Well, the love I want most is...

749
00:41:10,250 --> 00:41:11,250
a family,

750
00:41:11,958 --> 00:41:13,041
a noodle stall.

751
00:41:13,958 --> 00:41:14,958
[inhales]

752
00:41:15,458 --> 00:41:16,541
Dad makes food.

753
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:18,999
Mom waits tables.

754
00:41:19,000 --> 00:41:20,207
[gentle music playing]

755
00:41:20,208 --> 00:41:22,625
And the kid helps out at home.

756
00:41:25,375 --> 00:41:27,208
I felt this kind of love once before.

757
00:41:28,208 --> 00:41:29,208
It's unforgettable.

758
00:41:29,875 --> 00:41:31,208
And later on, it...

759
00:41:31,875 --> 00:41:33,791
it took a long, long time to...

760
00:41:35,333 --> 00:41:36,458
accept that this love...

761
00:41:38,708 --> 00:41:40,541
had gradually disappeared on me.

762
00:41:48,875 --> 00:41:51,415
[chuckles] I'm sorry about that.
Hey, another toast.

763
00:41:51,416 --> 00:41:54,665
Everyone, enjoy yourselves.
It's my treat, yeah?

764
00:41:54,666 --> 00:41:55,832
[glasses clink]

765
00:41:55,833 --> 00:41:56,916
[all] Cheers.

766
00:41:58,166 --> 00:42:01,333
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

767
00:42:05,250 --> 00:42:07,458
[Yu-hua] Stop worrying about your paper.

768
00:42:09,625 --> 00:42:10,625
What are you doing back?

769
00:42:12,750 --> 00:42:15,624
I've... got that hearing tomorrow.

770
00:42:15,625 --> 00:42:17,333
I wanted to go over some things.

771
00:42:18,250 --> 00:42:19,250
Ah... [chuckles]

772
00:42:21,250 --> 00:42:22,500
- [inhales]
- [Cheng-chun] When you--

773
00:42:23,750 --> 00:42:25,415
[both chuckle]

774
00:42:25,416 --> 00:42:28,500
Earlier, that was something.

775
00:42:29,250 --> 00:42:32,165
- To run into each other on the street.
- [chuckling] Ah, yeah.

776
00:42:32,166 --> 00:42:33,540
- It was.
- [Yu-hua] Mmm.

777
00:42:33,541 --> 00:42:35,333
- That was something.
- [Yu-hua] Mmm.

778
00:42:38,375 --> 00:42:40,500
[breathes heavily]

779
00:42:41,750 --> 00:42:42,958
Did you know that...

780
00:42:43,875 --> 00:42:46,791
the kid we treated
for cardiac tamponade earlier

781
00:42:47,583 --> 00:42:48,875
didn't pull through?

782
00:42:50,750 --> 00:42:53,000
[somber music playing]

783
00:42:53,958 --> 00:42:54,958
I heard.

784
00:42:56,791 --> 00:43:00,875
We got it diagnosed so fast,
and our patients are...

785
00:43:02,541 --> 00:43:03,874
on the brink.

786
00:43:03,875 --> 00:43:07,165
We give medicine, treatment, surgery,

787
00:43:07,166 --> 00:43:09,791
everything we can to save them.

788
00:43:12,666 --> 00:43:14,000
Sometimes, they...

789
00:43:15,625 --> 00:43:16,625
they still die.

790
00:43:17,208 --> 00:43:19,291
[sighs] That's life.

791
00:43:21,291 --> 00:43:22,458
It's how it is...

792
00:43:23,250 --> 00:43:24,625
in the ER, right?

793
00:43:29,458 --> 00:43:30,458
[chuckles softly]

794
00:43:41,708 --> 00:43:45,665
On February 4, 2023,
the complainant's wife went to the ER.

795
00:43:45,666 --> 00:43:48,665
She had been vomiting,
and died during her treatment.

796
00:43:48,666 --> 00:43:52,207
He Yu-hua, you're facing charges
of negligent homicide.

797
00:43:52,208 --> 00:43:55,833
Please describe the treatment you gave
that day with as much detail as possible.

798
00:44:01,583 --> 00:44:05,874
The patient had been vomiting,
and her blood pressure was high.

799
00:44:05,875 --> 00:44:08,374
- [panting]
- Ms. Lin, you're dehydrated.

800
00:44:08,375 --> 00:44:10,249
We'll treat you for the nausea.

801
00:44:10,250 --> 00:44:13,999
If you're still not feeling well,
you need to let us know.

802
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:15,541
After that initial treatment,

803
00:44:16,250 --> 00:44:18,582
the patient reported an improvement.

804
00:44:18,583 --> 00:44:21,665
Later on, she suddenly fell unconscious

805
00:44:21,666 --> 00:44:23,457
- <i>and had a seizure.</i>
- [machine beeping rapidly]

806
00:44:23,458 --> 00:44:26,290
- [gasping]
- [Hsiu-ju] Okay.

807
00:44:26,291 --> 00:44:28,333
- [Yu-hua] IV, hurry.
- [Hsiu-ju] Yep.

808
00:44:30,208 --> 00:44:31,415
Anticonvulsants injected.

809
00:44:31,416 --> 00:44:34,915
[Yu-hua] <i>Her blood pressure was still high
which pointed to eclampsia.</i>

810
00:44:34,916 --> 00:44:37,124
<i>I immediately consulted with an OBGYN.</i>

811
00:44:37,125 --> 00:44:40,708
The fetal heart rate
was only between 50 to 60.

812
00:44:41,458 --> 00:44:43,165
But the situation was very serious.

813
00:44:43,166 --> 00:44:45,916
The OBGYN decided to perform a C-section.

814
00:44:46,916 --> 00:44:49,415
The child... could not be saved.

815
00:44:49,416 --> 00:44:51,333
And the patient died as well.

816
00:44:52,583 --> 00:44:55,915
I have a report here
from the Medical Review Committee,

817
00:44:55,916 --> 00:45:00,332
which indicates the attending physician
failed to check for brainstem hemorrhage,

818
00:45:00,333 --> 00:45:02,957
which cannot be ruled out
as contributing to the patient's death.

819
00:45:02,958 --> 00:45:04,499
The patient had a seizure.

820
00:45:04,500 --> 00:45:07,290
Doctor, are these the symptoms
of a brainstem hemorrhage?

821
00:45:07,291 --> 00:45:09,499
Yes, but also of eclampsia.

822
00:45:09,500 --> 00:45:11,583
Did you examine her
for a brainstem hemorrhage?

823
00:45:14,541 --> 00:45:17,458
Did you arrange for a CT scan
to be undertaken?

824
00:45:18,416 --> 00:45:19,624
[sighs heavily]

825
00:45:19,625 --> 00:45:21,708
[suspenseful music playing]

826
00:45:22,666 --> 00:45:23,666
[sobbing]

827
00:45:29,250 --> 00:45:31,291
- [Yu-hua breathing heavily]
- [machine beeping rapidly]

828
00:45:34,583 --> 00:45:37,249
[Yu-hua] <i>The patient was suffering
concurrent seizures.</i>

829
00:45:37,250 --> 00:45:40,415
This is a very strong indicator
of pre-eclampsia,

830
00:45:40,416 --> 00:45:42,957
which is extremely dangerous
for the patient and the baby.

831
00:45:42,958 --> 00:45:44,749
You didn't answer my question.

832
00:45:44,750 --> 00:45:47,582
You failed to diagnose
any brainstem hemorrhage.

833
00:45:47,583 --> 00:45:51,291
And did not arrange for a CT scan.
Is this true or not?

834
00:45:55,500 --> 00:45:56,500
It's true.

835
00:45:57,000 --> 00:45:58,000
[whimpers]

836
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:00,000
[sniffles]

837
00:46:03,166 --> 00:46:05,291
- [Yu-hua panting]
- [machine beeping rapidly]

838
00:46:12,166 --> 00:46:13,290
[whimpering]

839
00:46:13,291 --> 00:46:16,540
<i>Mr. Yu, I'm so sorry. We did our best.</i>

840
00:46:16,541 --> 00:46:19,083
No, you need to save her!

841
00:46:20,291 --> 00:46:21,582
[cell phone vibrates]

842
00:46:21,583 --> 00:46:23,457
CHENG-CHUN

843
00:46:23,458 --> 00:46:26,082
[Mr. Yu] <i>I'm begging you, doctor!</i>

844
00:46:26,083 --> 00:46:27,874
I can't do this!

845
00:46:27,875 --> 00:46:29,665
- Please!
- There's nothing...

846
00:46:29,666 --> 00:46:33,582
[judge] <i>He Yu-hua, if you had arranged
for the patient to have a CT scan,</i>

847
00:46:33,583 --> 00:46:36,249
<i>is it possible
that you could've prevented this?</i>

848
00:46:36,250 --> 00:46:39,208
- [cell phone vibrating]
- [sobbing]

849
00:46:42,041 --> 00:46:43,958
CHENG-CHUN

850
00:46:46,041 --> 00:46:47,707
[motorcycle honking]

851
00:46:47,708 --> 00:46:49,540
- [gasps, screams]
- [tires screeching]

852
00:46:49,541 --> 00:46:51,916
- [Yu-hua groans]
- [civilians exclaim, grunts]

853
00:46:52,958 --> 00:46:54,958
- [breath trembling]
- [cell phone vibrating]

854
00:46:57,708 --> 00:47:00,458
- [rain pattering]
- [gasps]

855
00:47:03,875 --> 00:47:05,875
[closing theme music playing]
